  "duration": 51.161,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.073,
      "text": "Does a full moon really trigger human madness?",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Full moon by Ram Samudrala.jpg",
        "credit": "Ram samudrala",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Full_moon_by_Ram_Samudrala.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.073,
      "end": 8.968,
      "text": "For centuries, medical staff and police have blamed the lunar cycle for spikes in chaos.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "MarkhamStouffvilleHospital23.jpg",
        "credit": "Raysonho @ Open Grid Scheduler / Grid Engine",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MarkhamStouffvilleHospital23.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.067,
          "end": 6.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 6.467,
          "end": 8.967,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 8.968,
      "end": 15.463,
      "text": "However, meta-analyses of over one hundred studies show zero correlation with human behavior.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Wages-relative-to-the-price-of-energy (OWID 1122).png",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wages-relative-to-the-price-of-energy_(OWID_1122).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 8.967,
          "end": 15.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.463,
      "end": 21.963,
      "text": "Even the twenty-eight day human cycle is a mismatch for the twenty-nine point five day lunar month.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Luteiniseeriv hormoon (LH) menstruaal tsy\u00fckli ajal.png",
        "credit": "Mikael H\u00e4ggstr\u00f6m",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luteiniseeriv_hormoon_(LH)_menstruaal_tsy%C3%BCkli_ajal.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 15.467,
          "end": 18.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 18.0,
          "end": 21.967,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 21.963,
      "end": 28.383,
      "text": "Research finds no link between moon phases and birth rates, homicide, or the number of suicides.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "BTP Peugeot at Kings Cross 01.jpg",
        "credit": "HJ Mitchell",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BTP_Peugeot_at_Kings_Cross_01.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 21.967,
          "end": 25.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 25.167,
          "end": 28.367,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.383,
      "end": 34.878,
      "text": "While the moon pulls entire oceans, its gravity is far too weak to impact human physiology.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Flickr via Openverse",
        "title": "Fogarty beach, Oregon",
        "credit": "Bonnie Moreland (free images)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://www.flickr.com/photos/66741228@N05/49225506951"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.367,
          "end": 34.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.878,
      "end": 40.373,
      "text": "Higher tides at the full moon occur because the Sun, Earth, and Moon align in space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Rhythms and Clocks in Marine Organisms Figure 1 Solar and Lunar Cycles ma150509.f1.jpg",
        "credit": "Image in panel a created by Reto Stockli with the help of Alan Nelson, under the leadership of Fritz Hasler, and reproduced from NASA's Visible Earth catalog (https://visibleearth.nasa.gov/images/5438",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rhythms_and_Clocks_in_Marine_Organisms_Figure_1_Solar_and_Lunar_Cycles_ma150509.f1.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.867,
          "end": 37.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 37.6,
          "end": 40.367,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.373,
      "end": 46.748,
      "text": "Coral species sync their lives to moonlight, but human actions remain grounded in science.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Coral polyps out at night at Fanous East Reef, Red Sea, Egypt -SCUBA -UNDERWATER -PICTURES (6522132607).jpg",
        "credit": "Derek Keats from Johannesburg, South Africa",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coral_polyps_out_at_night_at_Fanous_East_Reef,_Red_Sea,_Egypt_-SCUBA_-UNDERWATER_-PICTURES_(6522132607).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.367,
          "end": 46.733,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 46.748,
      "end": 50.811,
      "text": "Yet despite zero scientific proof, the ancient myth survives.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Full moon by Ram Samudrala.jpg",
        "credit": "Ram samudrala",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
